 "text": "Services | Dallas County, IA\nSkip To Main Content This website is AudioEye enabled and is being optimized for accessibility. To open the AudioEye Toolbar, press \"shift + =\". Some assistive technologies may require the use of a passthrough function before this keystroke. For more information, activate the button labeled \"Explore your accessibility options\".\nLoading\nSkip to Main Content\nCreate a Website Account - Manage notification subscriptions, save form progress and more.\nWebsite Sign In\nSearch\nGovernment\nServices\nOur Community\nHow Do I...\nHome\nServices\nServices\nThe essential services the County provides are designed to make Dallas County a safe, healthy, and fulfilling place to live, work and play. Community members interact with the County government daily through services such as vaccination clinics, social services assistance and mental health services. The County also has a wide range of conservation opportunities, county parks, land and water trails and so much more!\nWhether you're visiting for the day or looking for a place to call home, you'll love all that Dallas County has to offer!\n9\n1\n1\n2\nBusiness Services\nAccess business services including building permits, mapping, zoning, and more.\nConservation\nthe Conservation department is responsible for protecting, managing, and maintaining natural resources, parks, and wildlife in Dallas County\nHealth & Social Services\nView services for families, persons with disabilities, the elderly, low-income families, and so much more.\nResident Services\nDiscover services for Dallas County residents.\nBusiness Services\nBuilding Permits & Codes\nEnvironmental Health Services\nGIS & Mapping\nGreater Dallas County Development Alliance\nProperty Information\nProperty Tax\nZoning\nConservation\nParks & Recreation\nEnvironmental Education\nPrairie Awakening\nVolunteer With Us!\nPublic Programs\nWilderness Trek\nAbout Us\nBoard of Directors\nMinutes and Agenda\nSpecial Events Policy and Ap